  <!-- Real operational note instead of generic feature grid / comparison table -->
  <h2>Two Details Most SimLocal Write-Ups Skip</h2>
  <p>
    SimLocal sells <strong>student-specific eSIM plans</strong> alongside its regular country and regional options, priced for longer stays rather than a short trip. If you're heading somewhere for a semester rather than a week, it's worth checking those instead of a standard tourist plan built around a shorter validity window.
  </p>
  <p>
    It also runs a small footprint of physical stores at a handful of airports, on top of the app and website. Most competitors on this site are app-and-browser only, so a staffed counter is a genuine point of difference if you'd rather have someone walk you through setup in person than follow a help article at 30,000 feet.
  </p>
  <p>
    The app itself can hold up to 10 stored eSIM profiles on one device, which matters if you keep old destination eSIMs around instead of deleting them after every trip.
  </p>

